  "name": "ANGIOTENSIN CONVERTING ENZYME (ACE)",
  "code": "0016",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"173\" data-end=\"598\">The <strong data-start=\"177\" data-end=\"216\">ACE (Angiotensin-Converting Enzyme)</strong> test measures the level of ACE in the blood. ACE is an enzyme that plays a role in the <strong data-start=\"304\" data-end=\"332\">renin-angiotensin system</strong>, which regulates blood pressure by converting angiotensin I to angiotensin II (a vasoconstrictor). Clinically, the ACE test is <strong data-start=\"460\" data-end=\"511\">most commonly used to help diagnose and monitor</strong> <strong data-start=\"512\" data-end=\"527\">sarcoidosis</strong>, a granulomatous disease that often affects the lungs and lymph nodes.</p>\n<p data-start=\"600\" data-end=\"818\">It may also be elevated in other granulomatous or inflammatory conditions. The test is not specific, but when interpreted with clinical findings and imaging, it supports the diagnosis and monitoring of such conditions.</p>\n<p data-start=\"858\" data-end=\"892\">High levels of ACE may indicate:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"893\" data-end=\"1206\">\n<li data-start=\"893\" data-end=\"983\">\n<p data-start=\"895\" data-end=\"983\"><strong data-start=\"895\" data-end=\"910\">Sarcoidosis</strong> &ndash; most common association; active disease typically shows elevated ACE</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"984\" data-end=\"1083\">\n<p data-start=\"986\" data-end=\"1028\"><strong data-start=\"986\" data-end=\"1018\">Other granulomatous diseases</strong>, such as:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1031\" data-end=\"1083\">\n<li data-start=\"1031\" data-end=\"1050\">\n<p data-start=\"1033\" data-end=\"1050\">Tuberculosis (TB)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1053\" data-end=\"1062\">\n<p data-start=\"1055\" data-end=\"1062\">Leprosy</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1065\" data-end=\"1083\">\n<p data-start=\"1067\" data-end=\"1083\">Histoplasmosis</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1084\" data-end=\"1107\">\n<p data-start=\"1086\" data-end=\"1107\"><strong data-start=\"1086\" data-end=\"1107\">Gaucher&rsquo;s disease</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1108\" data-end=\"1129\">\n<p data-start=\"1110\" data-end=\"1129\"><strong data-start=\"1110\" data-end=\"1129\">Hyperthyroidism</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1130\" data-end=\"1172\">\n<p data-start=\"1132\" data-end=\"1172\"><strong data-start=\"1132\" data-end=\"1155\">Diabetic neuropathy</strong> (occasionally)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1173\" data-end=\"1206\">\n<p data-start=\"1175\" data-end=\"1206\"><strong data-start=\"1175\" data-end=\"1206\">Primary biliary cholangitis</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"1208\" data-end=\"1428\">However, ACE levels can be elevated in <strong data-start=\"1247\" data-end=\"1270\">healthy individuals</strong>, and some patients with sarcoidosis may have normal ACE levels. Therefore, it&rsquo;s best used in conjunction with other diagnostic tools like imaging and biopsy.</p>",
